WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:03.860
In part one

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.980
we solved the rooms with eigenvectors.

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.700
Each part of the solution behaves

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.620
like e to the lambda t.

5
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.340
A negative lambda makes it decay.

6
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.461
A positive lambda makes

7
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:18.231
it grow without bound.

8
00:00:18.308 --> 00:00:20.618
And lambda equal to zero makes

9
00:00:20.695 --> 00:00:22.850
it stay exactly where it is.

10
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.176
So what decides whether every

11
00:00:26.278 --> 00:00:28.536
solution settles down?

12
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:30.280
Pause and think.

13
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.775
Take away the outside walls.

14
00:00:36.775 --> 00:00:40.883
The rooms only trade heat with each other

15
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:43.940
minus one, one, one, minus one.

16
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.463
Now one, one has eigenvalue zero

17
00:00:47.463 --> 00:00:50.828
equal rooms have nothing to trade.

18
00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:54.290
One, minus one still has minus two.

19
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.872
Start at ten, zero, and run the flow.

20
00:00:57.872 --> 00:01:01.016
The difference dies, the sum stays

21
00:01:01.016 --> 00:01:04.946
and the point comes to rest on the diagonal

22
00:01:04.946 --> 00:01:08.440
at five and five: the average, forever.

23
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.330
A third design

24
00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:13.649
room one gets a heater that adds heat

25
00:01:13.736 --> 00:01:16.619
in proportion to its temperature.

26
00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:20.374
The matrix is zero, one, one, minus three

27
00:01:20.374 --> 00:01:22.820
with determinant minus one.

28
00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.215
A negative determinant means eigenvalues

29
00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:29.108
of opposite signs: about point three

30
00:01:29.108 --> 00:01:31.316
and minus three point three.

31
00:01:31.316 --> 00:01:34.437
Watch a point near the stable direction.

32
00:01:34.437 --> 00:01:36.797
It first falls in, then turns

33
00:01:36.797 --> 00:01:39.690
and runs away along the unstable one.

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.986
For a two by two matrix

35
00:01:42.071 --> 00:01:43.933
there is a quick test

36
00:01:44.018 --> 00:01:47.487
stable exactly when the trace is negative

37
00:01:47.572 --> 00:01:50.280
and the determinant is positive.

38
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.457
A mass on a spring, with no friction

39
00:01:54.457 --> 00:01:57.762
the acceleration of y is minus y.

40
00:01:57.859 --> 00:02:01.164
Keep the position and the velocity

41
00:02:01.261 --> 00:02:03.497
together in one vector.

42
00:02:03.497 --> 00:02:07.580
The matrix is zero, one, minus one, zero.

43
00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:11.471
Its eigenvalues are i and minus i.

44
00:02:11.471 --> 00:02:15.741
Complex eigenvalues mean the flow turns.

45
00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:20.428
Start at one, zero, and the point goes round

46
00:02:20.532 --> 00:02:25.010
and round the circle, for ever: y is cos t.

47
00:02:26.423 --> 00:02:27.807
Add friction.

48
00:02:27.807 --> 00:02:32.170
The matrix becomes zero, one, minus two

49
00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.108
minus two, and the eigenvalues minus

50
00:02:36.214 --> 00:02:38.343
one plus or minus i.

51
00:02:38.693 --> 00:02:42.740
The imaginary part still turns the point.

52
00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.589
The real part, minus one, pulls it in.

53
00:02:46.589 --> 00:02:50.439
Each half second it turns and shrinks

54
00:02:50.439 --> 00:02:52.413
a spiral into rest.

55
00:02:52.763 --> 00:02:55.519
The position is e to the minus t

56
00:02:55.519 --> 00:02:57.524
times cos t plus sin t

57
00:02:57.524 --> 00:03:00.615
point five zero eight at one second

58
00:03:00.615 --> 00:03:02.536
and small steps agree.

59
00:03:02.536 --> 00:03:04.958
The eigenvalues are complex

60
00:03:04.958 --> 00:03:06.963
but the answer is real.

61
00:03:07.543 --> 00:03:12.076
One matrix does all of this: e to the A t.

62
00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:16.933
For a number, e to the a t is one, plus a t

63
00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:21.035
plus a t squared over two, and so on.

64
00:03:21.035 --> 00:03:22.546
For a matrix

65
00:03:22.546 --> 00:03:26.863
take the same series as the definition.

66
00:03:27.213 --> 00:03:30.342
When A is X lambda X inverse

67
00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:35.198
every power is too, so the series becomes X

68
00:03:35.198 --> 00:03:38.435
e to the lambda t, X inverse

69
00:03:38.435 --> 00:03:41.995
exponentials of the eigenvalues

70
00:03:41.995 --> 00:03:44.693
in the eigenvector grid.

71
00:03:45.043 --> 00:03:47.499
For the rooms at half an hour

72
00:03:47.499 --> 00:03:49.791
thirty terms of the series

73
00:03:49.791 --> 00:03:51.347
the eigen-formula

74
00:03:51.347 --> 00:03:54.458
and the computer's routine all agree.

75
00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:55.931
It has moved ten

76
00:03:55.931 --> 00:03:58.223
zero to two point five two

77
00:03:58.223 --> 00:04:00.843
one point one six, in one step.

78
00:04:01.423 --> 00:04:04.143
Here is a tempting shortcut

79
00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:08.223
take e to the power of each entry of A t?

80
00:04:08.803 --> 00:04:11.954
For the rooms at half an hour that gives

81
00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:15.026
zero point two two on the diagonal and

82
00:04:15.105 --> 00:04:17.153
one point six five off it.

83
00:04:17.153 --> 00:04:20.382
Start with two degrees in room one only.

84
00:04:20.461 --> 00:04:22.982
The fake matrix puts three point

85
00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:25.266
three degrees into room two

86
00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:26.763
heat from nowhere.

87
00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:30.196
The true flow sends the same start to

88
00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.113
about half a degree and a quarter.

89
00:04:33.113 --> 00:04:35.030
Use the eigen-formula

90
00:04:35.113 --> 00:04:37.113
or a library routine for

91
00:04:37.196 --> 00:04:39.113
the matrix exponential.

92
00:04:39.693 --> 00:04:42.959
Training a model moves its weights

93
00:04:43.055 --> 00:04:44.880
downhill on a loss.

94
00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.338
For a quadratic bowl with matrix H

95
00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:51.795
moving continuously downhill is the

96
00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.773
flow d w d t equals minus H w.

97
00:04:55.123 --> 00:04:59.598
Our H has eigenvalue ten along one, one

98
00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.164
a steep wall.

99
00:05:01.164 --> 00:05:06.199
And one along one, minus one: a flat valley.

100
00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:09.555
Run the flow from three, one.

101
00:05:09.555 --> 00:05:13.807
It drops off the wall almost at once

102
00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:17.163
then creeps along the valley.

103
00:05:17.513 --> 00:05:19.747
Gradient descent is Euler's

104
00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.567
method for this flow

105
00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:24.960
with the learning rate as the time step.

106
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.614
At point zero five

107
00:05:26.614 --> 00:05:29.593
the steps follow the valley safely.

108
00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:32.278
But step factors are one minus

109
00:05:32.356 --> 00:05:34.380
ten eta and one minus eta.

110
00:05:34.457 --> 00:05:36.792
At point two one the steep one

111
00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.660
is minus one point one

112
00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.929
and the weights bounce from wall to wall

113
00:05:41.929 --> 00:05:43.408
further each time.

114
00:05:43.486 --> 00:05:45.743
The steepest direction limits

115
00:05:45.821 --> 00:05:48.623
the learning rate: below two tenths.

116
00:05:49.203 --> 00:05:50.661
So, to sum up

117
00:05:50.765 --> 00:05:54.202
the real parts of the eigenvalues

118
00:05:54.306 --> 00:05:57.951
decide in or out: negative settles

119
00:05:57.951 --> 00:06:01.283
zero rests, positive runs away.

120
00:06:01.633 --> 00:06:05.315
The imaginary parts make the flow turn.

121
00:06:05.315 --> 00:06:09.375
And all of it is one matrix, e to the A t

122
00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:12.113
built from the eigenvectors.

123
00:06:12.693 --> 00:06:13.737
Next lecture

124
00:06:13.737 --> 00:06:17.108
matrices whose columns are probabilities.

125
00:06:17.108 --> 00:06:20.400
Their largest eigenvalue is exactly one

126
00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.728
and its eigenvector is where

127
00:06:22.808 --> 00:06:24.333
everything settles.
